# Nova Elite Homes — Investor Portal & Admin Console
## Product Requirements Document (PRD) for Engineering

**Status:** Draft for implementation
**Scope:** Investor Portal + Admin Console only (marketing site is out of scope — already complete)
**Stack:** Next.js (App Router) + React + Tailwind + Firebase (Auth, Firestore, Storage)

---

## 1. Purpose & Context

Nova Elite Homes is a London property / short-let portfolio company. This PRD covers the two authenticated surfaces of the product:

- **Investor Portal** — where investors log in and view their own portfolio performance, read-only.
- **Admin Console** — internal tool where Nova staff manage investor data, which then flows through to what investors see.

The marketing site and Firebase Auth wiring already exist. This document defines what "done" means for the two authenticated surfaces so it can be handed to an implementation agent (Cursor) as a build spec.

---

## 2. Goals

1. Investors can securely log in and see an accurate, real-time view of their own portfolio — and only their own.
2. Admins can onboard and update investor data (financials, properties, bookings, analytics) without touching code or redeploying.
3. Firestore security rules enforce the read/write boundaries described in this doc — not just UI-level checks.
4. Replace remaining placeholder/demo chart data with real Firestore-backed data.
5. Light/dark mode persists per user across sessions.

### Non-goals (this phase)
- Payments / investor fund transfers.
- Automated ingestion from booking platforms (Airbnb, Booking.com, etc.) — manual admin entry only, for now.
- Multi-admin roles / permission tiers beyond a single admin flag.
- Native mobile app.

---

## 3. Roles & Access Model

| Role | Identified by | Access |
|---|---|---|
| Public visitor | Unauthenticated | Marketing site only |
| Investor | Firebase Auth user with an investor profile doc | Read own profile, own properties, own bookings, own analytics. No write access. |
| Admin | Firebase Auth user whose email matches an admin allowlist (Firestore `admins` collection, not hardcoded) | Full read/write on all investors and their subcollections |

**Important implementation note:** the brief describes admin as "a configured admin email" (singular, hardcoded). Recommend implementing this as a Firestore-backed `admins/{uid}` collection (or custom claims) from day one rather than a hardcoded string in code, since a hardcoded email is a security anti-pattern and doesn't survive the "exact admin access model" open question in the brief. Custom claims (via a Firebase Admin SDK callable function) are the more secure long-term answer, but a Firestore `admins` collection is an acceptable v1 if custom claims add too much scope — either way, **do not hardcode an email string into security rules or client code**.

