## 4. Data Model (Firestore)

```
investors/{investorId}
  - uid: string (Firebase Auth UID, == doc id)
  - name: string
  - email: string
  - totalInvested: number
  - totalReturns: number
  - portfolioValue: number
  - createdAt: timestamp
  - updatedAt: timestamp

investors/{investorId}/properties/{propertyId}
  - name: string
  - address: string
  - imageUrls: string[]  (Storage refs)
  - status: enum (active | inactive | sold)
  - purchasePrice: number
  - currentValue: number
  - createdAt / updatedAt: timestamp

investors/{investorId}/bookings/{bookingId}
  - propertyId: string (ref)
  - startDate: timestamp
  - endDate: timestamp
  - guestName: string (optional)
  - revenue: number
  - channel: enum (direct | airbnb | booking.com | other)
  - status: enum (confirmed | pending | cancelled)

investors/{investorId}/analytics/{periodId}
  - period: string (e.g. "2026-07")
  - revenue: number
  - commission: number
  - occupancyRate: number
  - channelBreakdown: map<string, number>

admins/{uid}
  - email: string
  - addedAt: timestamp
```

**Open decision (flag to product owner, don't silently assume):** whether `analytics` docs are pre-aggregated by admin/a scheduled function, or computed client-side from `bookings`. Recommend pre-aggregated (admin-entered or Cloud Function–derived) for performance and simplicity, since bookings could grow large per investor. This PRD assumes pre-aggregated analytics docs.

